# snow-cuffs standing rules — append this block to your project AGENTS.md.
# Wording is imperative: these are instructions to the agent, not docs.

## snow-cuffs Cost Governance

### Retrieval before reading
- Before opening more than 2 files, query `SNOWCUFFS.CODE_INDEX.TEAM_CODE_SEARCH`
  (`SNOWFLAKE.CORTEX.SEARCH_PREVIEW`, limit 5) and read only the returned chunks.
  Open a full file only when a chunk is insufficient; prefer ranged reads.
- Never paste whole files into a prompt when a chunk answers the question.

### Data questions
- Run `$dbq` first: schema cards via `SNOWCUFFS.DB_CONTEXT.DB_SCHEMA_SEARCH`.
  Never crawl `INFORMATION_SCHEMA` or `SHOW TABLES` across databases.
- Prefer Cortex Analyst when a semantic model covers the domain.

### Batch AI SQL
- Run `$preflight` before any `AI_*` function over a table (not a literal).
  Above the gate (default 5 credits) stop for explicit user confirmation.
- Always run a `LIMIT 20` quality probe before a full-table AI run.

### Model tiering
- Default every Cortex LLM call to `SNOWCUFFS.PUBLIC.CHEAPEST_MODEL_FOR_TIER`
  of the smallest capable tier: 'small' for classification/extraction/routing,
  'medium' for >5k-token summarization, 'large' only for multi-step reasoning
  or after a smaller model demonstrably failed the same task this session.

### Session hygiene
- Start with `$warmstart`; cite the context pack instead of re-deriving it.
- Do not re-read files already in context unless they changed.
- One precise search beats several broad ones; on long tasks, summarize
  progress and drop stale context rather than carrying full history forward.
